'''Aipi''' ({{Literal translation|gathering place}}) is the largest [[W:Artificial lake|artificial lake]] and [[W:Reservoir (water)|reservoir]] by [[W:List of reservoirs by volume|volume]] in [[Balisca]]. It lies {{convert|298|km|mi}} upstream from the mouth of the [[Tapajós river]] on the [[W:Argentine Sea|Baliscan (Argentine) Sea]], within the bounds of the [[Bayara|Bayaran]] community. The [[W:Depression (geology)|depression]] which Aipi occupies was filled between 1961 and 1968 following the completion of the Tapajós Dam project. 

The planned community of [[Vilaxoyosa]] was built for the construction workers of the diversion project.
